 :findings [{:id :manifest-binding-not-specified :severity :planning-blocker
             :evidence "Plan lines 47-56 output only payload and descriptor, with an independently supplied binding; r01/r03 mention a digest/hash but do not define an artifact record or its independent validation. S1A generation.cljc lines 225-254 produces and checks closed artifact metadata, content SHA, UTF-8 byte count, format and validator identity/revision together against exact content. The proposed slice explicitly leaves S1A render-preview and format enum unchanged."
             :impact "A test of a hash alone does not bind the described bytes, format, descriptor and validator/source identity into a closed consumer artifact; the plan cannot yet establish the requested analogous manifest law. Nor can the distinct Services format be represented as an accepted existing S1A target."
             :required "Revise the plan to specify the exact closed standalone artifact/manifest data and independently checked relationships: format identity distinct from :oikos/profile-edn, exact payload SHA-256 and UTF-8 byte count, descriptor/value equality, and allowlisted validator/source binding. Give a canonical digest input or explicitly defer any generation-level digest rather than claiming S1A interoperability. Specify RED mutations for every field, altered payload/descriptor, extra keys and changed binding. Keep S1A target enum and renderer untouched; if this cannot fit the ceiling return for renewed review."
             :boundary "Do not add destination or claim an S1A target, Services policy FormatBinding, actual source-byte attestation or a completed generation merely to imitate the S1A record."}
            {:id :raw-byte-and-limits-contract-underspecified :severity :planning-blocker
             :evidence "Plan lines 53-55 demand a selected UTF-8 byte bound and invalid raw UTF-8 rejection but choose no bound or portable raw-byte input representation. digest.cljc utf8 and sha256 accept strings and encode them; frame/read-one also accepts strings, not arbitrary raw octets. Escaping can make output larger than the original value."
             :impact "The planned RED tests cannot unambiguously exercise malformed raw bytes or agreed boundary sizes across BB and NBB, and successful string round trips alone do not prove strict input decoding or raw byte/hash identity."
             :required "Specify a closed portable representation of octets and bounded strict UTF-8 decoding/round-trip equality before parsing or hashing, with how the digest is bound to those exact octets using available pure code. Choose concrete value and total rendered-payload byte ceilings, enforce them before expensive construction, and add RED tests at both boundaries, escape expansion, overlong encodings, isolated continuation bytes, truncated sequences and surrogate encodings in both runtimes. If this requires code beyond the three named paths or a new shared kernel, stop for renewed review rather than silently expanding scope."}]
